    "alert_id": "ALERT_001",
    "title": "EFV CNS toxicity: insomnia and vivid dreams",
    "message": "Guidelines list dizziness, insomnia, abnormal dreams, and mental symptoms including anxiety, depression, and suicidality as persistent CNS toxicity of EFV. For adults on EFV 600mg, recommended management is to lower the dose to EFV 400mg. For children, reassurance is advised first, with substitution to DTG or LPV/r if symptoms persist. Patient P003 reports poor sleep and vivid dreams for several weeks after starting EFV in February 2024, nearly two years ago. No suicidal ideation is present. These symptoms are classic EFV CNS side effects. No alternative non-drug cause is evident from the clinical notes. The clinician's plan documents the complaints but does not propose any intervention such as dose reduction or substitution.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Per guidelines, lower EFV dose from 600mg to 400mg. If symptoms persist after dose reduction, substitute EFV with DTG. Reassure patient and monitor for resolution.",
