      {"page_number": 36, "chunk_id": "hiv_guidelines_art.extraction__hiv_guidelines_art.extraction__p36_c1"},
      {"page_number": 39, "chunk_id": "hiv_guidelines_art.extraction__hiv_guidelines_art.extraction__p39_c1"},
      {"page_number": 5, "chunk_id": "hiv_guidelines_art.extraction__hiv_guidelines_art.extraction__p5_c3"}
    ]
  },
  {
    "alert_id": "ALERT_002",
    "title": "Missing TDF renal and bone monitoring labs",
    "message": "Guidelines state that for TDF toxicity (chronic kidney disease, acute kidney injury, Fanconi syndrome, decreased bone mineral density), clinicians should perform LFTs and RFTs, and if GFR is <60 mL/min or liver enzymes are elevated, substitute TDF with ABC. Patient P003 is on TDF but no renal function tests, liver function tests, or bone-related assessments appear in the recorded labs. The clinician's plan does not include any lab orders. Absence of baseline or routine renal monitoring in a patient on TDF represents a monitoring gap, as early detection of renal impairment is necessary to prevent TDF nephrotoxicity progression.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Order renal function tests (creatinine/eGFR) and liver function tests for patient on TDF. If GFR <60 mL/min, substitute TDF with ABC per guidelines.",
    "citations": [
      {"page_number": 37, "chunk_id": "hiv_guidelines_art.extraction__hiv_guidelines_art.extraction__p37_c1"}
    ]
  },
  {
    "alert_id": "ALERT_003",
    "title": "Viral load overdue per monitoring schedule",
    "message": "Guidelines recommend that for adults on ART, the first viral load should be done 6 months after initiation, the second at 12 months, and thereafter every 12 months if suppressed. Patient P003 started ART in February 2024. The most recent viral load was 60 copies/mL on 2025-08-10, approximately 18 months after initiation. The next scheduled viral load would have been due around 2026-08-10, which is 7 months after the current visit. However, the 12-month viral load (due around August 2025) appears to be the only result on record, and no viral load is planned in the clinician's orders. While not yet overdue, confirming the next VL date is important.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
    "severity": "low",
    "recommended_action": "Confirm next viral load is scheduled for approximately August 2026 per the 12-monthly adult monitoring schedule. Document the planned test date.",
    "citations": [
